  "body": "> Replaces #423, moved to the new fork (the old fork left NeoTech's network, and a push there closes the PR). Main is merged in. The two conflicts were module lists in `ui/src/state.rs` and `egui_app/tests.rs`, where both sides are kept (#371's tool_body). `setup_post_options` passes 8/8, the ui lib tests 11/11, and clippy for app and ui is clean. The hands-on GUI check is done (see the PR comments); since then main was merged again with a semantic per-op skip merge (#155 / #388).\n\n## What changed\n**Post options per setup** (same own / follow-the-document law #343 gave the post itself):\n- `SetupDef.post_options: Option<PostOptions>`; `None` follows the document (every older file and every new setup).\n- New undoable command `SetSetupPostOptions`; a no-op request is refused by name. A datum transfer copies the source setup's options with its post.\n- `posting::post_options` returns the active setup's own options, else the document's (mirrors `post_of`). \"Skip pauses and homes\" is read per operation from that op's setup, so one setup can skip its stops while another keeps them. Output (one file per op) and thread output are program-wide: setups that disagree are refused by name, next to #343's one-mount check.\n- Project file: an additive setup key `post_options` (`{\"threading\":\"g32\"|\"g76\",\"skip_stops\":..,\"per_op_files\":..}`), omitted when `None`; no version step (stays v57), so a document that never sets it saves byte-identically. An unknown threading word is a corrupt-file refusal naming the setup.\n- UI: the setup's **Post** page ends with a \"Post options\" group - radios \"Use the document's post options\" / \"This setup has its own post options\" and a note saying whose options the widgets above edit. The existing option widgets route to the active setup's own options when it has them.\n\n**Setup tool-list export**\n- `app::tool_list_export` (pure read): rows in first-use order from `tool_list::for_setup` - T number, name, diameter (mm), kind, holder (`D x L` or `none`), ops using it. `.csv` -> RFC 4180 CSV (CRLF, quoted fields); any other extension -> fixed-column text.\n- The setup's **Tool list** page gets an \"Export tool list…\" button (save dialog, CSV/Text filters, default `<Setup>-tools.csv`). A command-free file write like the setup sheet: nothing enters the history.\n\n## Readings\nDebug, M5 Mac. `scripts/gate.sh quick` (all camcraft-app + camcraft-ui suites): 1725 passed, 4 failed - all known reds on main: `setup_stock_source::a_new_block_after_a_flip…` (#415) and the GPU headless trio (`headless_run_succeeds`, `headless_cli_exit_code_is_zero`, `egui_headless_cli_exit_code_is_zero`). Goldens (`golden_cl` 23, posts) and `project_roundtrip` (69) unchanged. Clippy `-D warnings` clean on app + ui.\n\n## Pinning tests\n- App `crates/app/tests/setup_post_options.rs`: `a_setups_own_post_options_do_undo_redo`, `a_setup_that_skips_posts_without_its_stops_while_the_other_follows_the_document`, `setups_disagreeing_on_the_output_are_refused_by_name`, `a_single_setup_document_posts_byte_identically`, `own_post_options_round_trip_and_old_files_follow_the_document`, `a_datum_transfer_keeps_the_source_setups_post_options`, `the_tool_list_exports_as_csv_and_text`, `a_tool_list_field_with_a_comma_is_quoted`.\n- UI lib `egui_app::tests::setup_post_options`: `the_option_switches_land_on_the_active_setups_own_options`, `the_post_page_radio_gives_the_setup_its_own_options`, `the_tool_list_page_exports_the_setups_tools`.\n\n## Not exercised\nThe real rfd save dialog (tests write through `ToolListExportFile`); a per-setup G76 thread post end to end on Fanuc Lathe; one-file-per-op from a setup's own options (same `post_options` path `per_op_files` already covers). GUI checked by hand (tool-list export to .csv and .txt on `test-423.camproj`); the per-setup skip was checked on that same project through the branch's own commands - see the PR comments.\n\nPosted G-code: existing documents post byte-identically; output only differs for a setup that is given its own options.\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/389-setup-tool-list.md`.\n\nChangelog: A setup can carry its own post options (skip pauses and homes, output, thread output) or follow the document's; the setup's Tool list page exports its tools as CSV or text\n\nFixes #389\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n",
